WHAT: demote KNotifications unconditional find_package(Qt6 DBus REQUIRED)
      and find_package(Canberra REQUIRED) to optional.
WHY:  CMake binds AND tighter than OR, so the guard
      `if (NOT APPLE AND NOT ANDROID AND NOT WIN32 AND NOT HAIKU OR (WIN32 AND
      NOT WITH_SNORETOAST))` is all-true on WASI and the block fires. This is
      the ONE place in KCalc entire framework graph where DBus is not behind
      the USE_DBUS switch -- and it is a CMake bug rather than a code
      dependency: src/CMakeLists.txt already gates every DBus source on
      `if (HAVE_DBUS)` (:23-29, :62-65, :84) and every audio source on
      `if (TARGET Canberra::Canberra)` (:56-58, :98-99). With USE_DBUS=OFF and
      no Canberra target, ZERO sources need either package.
      This two-line change is what removes DBus from this port graph
      entirely, and it is the single highest-leverage patch in the series.
      WHAT IS LOST: notification SOUNDS. Canberra is libcanberra, an
      ALSA/PulseAudio event-sound player, and there is no wasm build of it. wk
      does have audio (plugins/audio-compat), so a real backend is possible
      later -- it just will not be libcanberra. Visual notifications are
      unaffected; on a platform with no notification server KNotification falls
      back to its own handling, which is what a wk node wants anyway.
UPSTREAM: as-is. The AND/OR precedence here is almost certainly not what the
      author meant, and the sources being correctly gated proves the packages
      were never meant to be REQUIRED.
diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 9135340..8fc8f9b 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -76,9 +76,21 @@ endif()
 
 find_package(KF6Config ${KF_DEP_VERSION} REQUIRED)
 
+# CMake binds AND tighter than OR, so on WASI the first conjunction is
+# all-true and this block fires -- demanding Qt6 DBus and Canberra
+# unconditionally, in the ONE framework in KCalc's graph where DBus is not
+# behind the USE_DBUS switch. It is a CMake bug, not a code dependency:
+# src/CMakeLists.txt gates every DBus source on `if (HAVE_DBUS)` (:23-29,
+# :62-65, :84) and every audio source on `if (TARGET Canberra::Canberra)`
+# (:56-58, :98-99), so with USE_DBUS=OFF and no Canberra target ZERO sources
+# need either. Making both non-REQUIRED removes DBus from this port's graph
+# entirely -- which is the single largest thing this patch series buys.
+# What is lost: notification SOUNDS (Canberra is libcanberra, an ALSA/
+# PulseAudio event-sound player). wk has audio via plugins/audio-compat, so a
+# real backend is possible later; it just is not libcanberra.
 if (NOT APPLE AND NOT ANDROID AND NOT WIN32 AND NOT HAIKU OR (WIN32 AND NOT WITH_SNORETOAST))
-    find_package(Qt6 ${REQUIRED_QT_VERSION} CONFIG REQUIRED DBus)
-    find_package(Canberra REQUIRED)
+    find_package(Qt6 ${REQUIRED_QT_VERSION} CONFIG QUIET COMPONENTS DBus)
+    find_package(Canberra)
     set_package_properties(Canberra PROPERTIES
         PURPOSE "Needed to build audio notification support")
     if (TARGET Canberra::Canberra)
